    ('FOAL', 'Young Equine', 'Young juvenile horse, pony, or donkey under one year of age.', 'Runs alongside its mother within hours of birth on long spindly legs.'),
    ('FOX', 'Cunning Canine', 'Small omnivorous mammal with a bushy tail, pointed snout, and keen hearing.', 'Can hear mice rustling beneath thick winter snow before pouncing with headfirst dives.'),
    ('FRIGATEBIRD', 'Pirate Seabird', 'Seabird where males inflate an enormous scarlet throat sac to attract mates.', 'Harasses other seabirds in mid-air until they disgorge freshly caught fish.'),
    ('FROG', 'Tailless Amphibian', 'Short-bodied, tailless amphibian with long hind legs adapted for jumping.', 'Absorbs water and oxygen directly through its permeable, moist skin.'),
    ('FULMAR', 'Arctic Seabird', 'Gull-like petrel that glides effortlessly above stormy northern ocean swells.', 'Defends cliffside nests by spitting noxious, foul-smelling stomach oil at intruders.'),
    ('GALLINULE', 'Purple Swamphen', 'Brilliantly colored wetland bird with rich purple-blue plumage and red shield.', 'Uses long toes to grasp food and climb through tangled floating aquatic plants.'),
    ('GANNET', 'Plunge Diver', 'Large seabird that plunge-dives into the ocean at 60 mph from 100 feet in air.', 'Features air-sac cushions in its face and chest to absorb high-speed water impact.'),
    ('GAR', 'Primitive Fish', 'Primitive freshwater fish with an elongated needle snout and diamond scales.', 'Equipped with ganoid armor scales and vascularized swim bladders for air.'),
    ('GAZELLE', 'Graceful Antelope', 'Small, swift antelope capable of running at high sustained speeds.', 'Evades cheetahs through zigzagging leaps and incredible agility across plains.'),
    ('GECKO', 'Wall-Climbing Lizard', 'Small nocturnal lizard with toe pads covered in microscopic hairs that stick to glass.', 'Utilizes van der Waals molecular forces to sprint upside down across smooth ceilings.'),
    ('GERBIL', 'Desert Rodent', 'Small hopping desert rodent adapted to arid climates with furry tails.', 'Produces minimal odorless urine and conserves water through efficient desert kidneys.'),
    ('GHARIAL', 'Fish-Eating Crocodilian', 'Fish-eating crocodilian with an extraordinarily long, slender needle-toothed snout.', 'Native to the northern Indian subcontinent; snatches fish with swift side-swipes.'),
    ('GIBBON', 'Lesser Ape', 'Small arboreal ape famous for swinging through forest canopies via brachiation.', 'Possesses ball-and-socket wrist joints allowing effortless tree branch swinging.'),
    ('GILAMONSTER', 'Venomous Lizard', 'Heavy, slow-moving lizard native to the American Southwest with beaded pink scales.', 'One of the few venomous lizards on Earth; grooved teeth channel venom into bites.'),
    ('GIRAFFE', 'Tallest Animal', 'The tallest living terrestrial animal, featuring an elongated neck and long legs.', 'Uses an 18-inch prehensile purplish-black tongue to strip leaves from thorny trees.'),
    ('GOAT', 'Sure-Footed Bovid', 'Agile horned herbivore capable of climbing steep mountain cliffs and dams.', 'Possesses horizontal rectangular pupils providing wide peripheral panoramic vision.'),
    ('GODWIT', 'Long-Billed Wader', 'Shorebird featuring a long, slightly upturned bill for probing deep in tidal mud.', 'The bar-tailed godwit flies non-stop 7,000 miles from Alaska to New Zealand.'),
    ('GOLDFINCH', 'Yellow Finch', 'Small songbird with bright yellow plumage and a black cap and wings.', 'Feeds voraciously on thistle seeds in open meadows and suburban gardens.'),
    ('GOOSE', 'V-Formation Migrator', 'Large waterfowl that flies in aerodynamic V-formations across continents in autumn.', 'Loudly honks while migrating to encourage lead flyers and maintain flock spacing.'),
    ('GOPHER', 'Burrowing Rodent', 'Fossorial burrowing rodent featuring large fur-lined external cheek pouches.', 'Excavates intricate tunnel networks, leaving characteristic horseshoe dirt mounds.'),
    ('GRASSHOPPER', 'Singing Jumper', 'Herbivorous insect with powerful jumping hind legs and chewing mouthparts.', 'Produces buzzing music by rubbing ridges on hind legs against wing edges.'),
    ('GREATDANE', 'Apollo of Dogs', 'One of the tallest dog breeds in the world, characterized by an imposing graceful stature.', 'Originally bred in Germany to hunt wild boar; gentle and affectionate with families.'),
    ('GREATWHITE', 'Apex Ocean Shark', 'Apex predatory shark possessing hundreds of triangular serrated teeth.', 'Can detect a single drop of blood in 25 million drops of water miles away.'),
    ('GREENFINCH', 'Olive Finch', 'Robust finch with olive-green plumage and bright yellow wing flashes.', 'Frequent visitor to garden seed feeders, singing wheezing twittering songs.'),
    ('GREENSHANK', 'Long-Legged Wader', 'Slender wading bird with long greenish legs and a slightly upturned bill.', 'Dashes swiftly through shallow tidal pools chasing small fish and shrimp.'),
    ('GREYHOUND', 'Sighthound Sprinter', 'Gentle, slender dog breed built for immense chasing speed and racing.', 'Can reach sprinting speeds exceeding 40 mph thanks to aerodynamic physiques.'),
    ('GRIZZLYBEAR', 'Brown Bear Subspecies', 'Massive apex bear recognized by a prominent muscular shoulder hump.', 'Excavates ground squirrel dens and snatches leaping salmon from Alaskan river falls.'),
    ('GROUPER', 'Heavy Reef Fish', 'Large-mouthed predatory fish that swallows prey whole by creating suction.', 'Goliath groupers can grow up to 8 feet in length and weigh over 800 pounds.'),
    ('GROUSE', 'Game Bird', 'Plump, ground-dwelling game bird inhabiting moorlands, prairies, and taiga.', 'Males perform elaborate communal courtship displays on open dancing grounds called leks.'),
    ('GUAN', 'Forest Bird', 'Large arboreal game bird inhabiting Central and South American cloud forests.', 'Known for loud wing-whirring displays made as it glides between tall trees.'),
    ('GUANACO', 'Wild Camelid', 'Wild South American camelid related to llamas that roams the arid Patagonian plains.', 'Can run at speeds of 35 mph across rocky Andean steppes to escape pumas.'),
    ('GUILLEMOT', 'Murre', 'Pelagic seabird that nests in dense colonies on tiny ledges of sea cliffs.', 'Lays pyriform pear-shaped eggs that roll in a tight circle rather than falling off cliffs.'),
    ('GUINEAFOWL', 'Polka-Dot Bird', 'African game bird with speckled grey-and-white plumage and a bony helmet casque.', 'Roams in noisy social flocks, sounding loud alarm clatter at approaching predators.'),
    ('GUINEAPIG', 'Cavy Pet', 'Domesticated South American rodent vocalizing through squeaks and whistles.', 'Originally domesticated by Andean indigenous peoples; requires dietary Vitamin C.'),
    ('GULL', 'Coastal Seabird', 'Omnivorous coastal seabird with grey and white plumage and keen scavenging habits.', 'Dives for fish and drops hard-shelled mollusks onto rocks to smash them open.'),
    ('HADDOCK', 'Marine Food Fish', "Marine fish belonging to the cod family marked by a black 'thumbprint' spot.", 'Important commercial catch in North Atlantic waters, popular in traditional fish and chips.'),
    ('HALIBUT', 'Giant Flatfish', 'The largest of all flatfish, capable of reaching over eight feet in length.', 'Demersal predator hunting cod, crabs, and squid on cold ocean seafloors.'),
    ('HAMERKOP', 'Hammerhead Stork', 'African water bird with an elongated backward-pointing crest resembling a hammer.', 'Constructs massive domed stick nests weighing up to 100 pounds in trees.'),
    ('HAMMERHEAD', 'Cephalofoil Shark', 'Shark recognized by the flattened hammer-shaped lateral extension of its head.', 'The wide hammer head provides panoramic 360-degree vision and electro-sensory reach.'),
    ('HAMSTER', 'Pocket Rodent', 'Small crepuscular rodent widely kept as a domestic pet with expandable cheeks.', 'Runs miles each night on exercise wheels and hoards seeds inside underground tunnels.'),
    ('HARE', 'Fast Lagomorph', 'Fast-running mammal with long ears and powerful hind legs built for sprinting.', 'Born fully furred with open eyes; relies on speed rather than burrows.'),
    ('HAWK', 'Woodland Raptor', 'Medium-sized bird of prey with broad wings and a long tail built for maneuvering.', 'Hunts small rodents, reptiles, and birds through dense forest tree lines.'),
    ('HEDGEHOG', 'Spiny Insectivore', 'Small nocturnal mammal covered in thousands of stiff, keratin-based defensive spines.', 'Curls into a spiny impenetrable ball when threatened, tucking in head and limbs.'),
    ('HELLBENDER', 'Giant Water Dog', 'Large aquatic salamander native to clear, rocky streams in eastern North America.', 'Breathes through loose, wrinkly skin folds that maximize oxygen uptake from water.'),
    ('HEN', 'Domestic Bird', 'Female domestic chicken kept worldwide for egg production and poultry meat.', 'Clucks softly to communicate with chicks before they hatch from shells.'),
    ('HERON', 'Patient Wader', 'Long-legged freshwater wading bird that stands motionless before spearing fish.', 'Strikes with lightning speed by extending its S-shaped neck forward like a spear.'),
    ('HERRING', 'Forage Fish', 'Silvery schooling forage fish that forms massive underwater bait balls.', 'Crucial keystone species feeding whales, dolphins, seabirds, seals, and sharks.'),
    ('HIPPO', 'River Giant', 'Heavy semi-aquatic African mammal that spends days submerged in fresh rivers.', 'Despite bulky appearance, can sprint 19 mph on land and possesses massive tusks.'),
    ('HIPPOPOTAMUS', 'River Giant', "Massive semi-aquatic African mammal that secretes a red 'blood sweat' sunscreen.", 'Possesses formidable canine tusks up to 20 inches long; highly territorial in rivers.'),
    ('HOATZIN', 'Stinkbird', 'Bizarre South American bird whose chicks possess functional wing claws.', 'Feeds strictly on leaves; ferments food in an enlarged crop smelling like cow manure.'),
    ('HONEYBEE', 'Social Pollinator', 'Social insect that produces golden honey, beeswax, and pollinates crops.', "Communicates the direction and distance to flower nectar using a complex 'waggle dance'."),
    ('HONEYEATER', 'Australian Nectar Bird', 'Diverse family of Australasian birds with brush-tipped tongues for nectar.', 'Major pollinators of eucalyptus, banksia, and grevillea flowering trees.'),
    ('HOOPOE', 'Crested Bird', 'Colorful bird with a dramatic fan-like crest of feathers and long curved bill.', 'Celebrated in ancient Egyptian and Persian mythology as a symbol of virtue.'),
    ('HORNET', 'Large Wasp', 'The largest eusocial wasp species, building papery carton nests in trees.', 'Can sting repeatedly without losing its stinger; aggressively defends nest colonies.'),
    ('HORSE', 'Equine Companion', 'Domesticated odd-toed ungulate that has served human transport and agriculture.', 'Can sleep both lying down and standing up thanks to a stay-apparatus lock.'),
    ('HUMMINGBIRD', 'Hovering Gem', 'Tiny bird capable of hovering in mid-air and flying backwards by beating wings 80 times/sec.', 'Feeds on flower nectar and possesses the fastest metabolism of any bird on Earth.'),
    ('HUSKY', 'Arctic Sled Dog', 'Thick-coated working sled dog breed originating from northeastern Siberia.', 'Bred by the Chukchi people; celebrated for striking blue eyes and howling.'),
    ('HYENA', 'Scavenger & Hunter', 'Carnivoran mammal famous for bone-crushing jaws and vocalizing laughing sounds.', 'Lives in complex matriarchal clans led by dominant females on African plains.'),
    ('HYRAX', 'Rock Dassie', 'Small, furry herbivorous mammal living in rocky outcrops across Africa.', 'Surprisingly, the hyrax is the closest living terrestrial evolutionary relative of the elephant!'),
    ('IBEX', 'Alpine Mountain Goat', 'Wild mountain goat with large curved ridged horns living on sheer cliffs.', 'Defies gravity by scaling nearly vertical rock faces and dams to lick mineral salts.'),
    ('IGUANA', 'Spiny Herbivorous Lizard', 'Large herbivorous lizard with a spiny crest running along its back and tail.', 'Marine iguanas in the Galapagos dive deep into cold ocean surf to graze on algae.'),
    ('IMPALA', 'Leaping Antelope', 'Medium-sized African antelope renowned for spectacular soaring leaps.', 'Can bound up to 30 feet in length and 10 feet in height to escape hunting wild dogs.'),
    ('INVERTEBRATE', 'Spineless Animal', 'Animal lacking a vertebral column or backbone, comprising 97% of all animal species.', 'Encompasses insects, mollusks, arachnids, jellyfish, crustaceans, and sponges.'),
    ('JACANA', 'Lotus Bird', 'Tropical wader possessing extraordinarily long toes enabling it to walk on floating lily pads.', "Often dubbed the 'Jesus bird' because it appears to walk directly on the surface of water."),
    ('JACKAL', 'African Wild Canine', 'Slender medium-sized wild canid native to Africa and southeastern Europe.', 'Adaptable opportunistic omnivore hunting small game and scavenging carrion.'),
    ('JAEGER', 'Parasitic Skua', 'Aggressive predatory seabird that steals caught fish from other flying birds.', 'Chases terns and gulls relentlessly until they drop or regurgitate their prey.'),
    ('JAGUAR', 'New World Big Cat', 'Compact muscular big cat native to the Americas with an exceptionally powerful bite.', 'Can pierce turtle shells and caiman armor; revered in ancient Mayan mythology.'),
    ('JAGUARUNDI', 'Otter Cat', 'Slender, unspotted wild cat native to the Americas with short legs and small ears.', 'Diurnal hunter that communicates through over a dozen bird-like whistle chirps.'),
    ('JAY', 'Corvid Bird', 'Noisy, brightly colored crested bird belonging to the intelligent crow family.', 'Blue jays bury acorns in forest floors, helping propagate oak woodland trees.'),
    ('JELLYFISH', 'Gelatinous Swimmer', 'Free-swimming marine animal with a gelatinous umbrella bell and trailing tentacles.', 'Lacks a brain, heart, and bones; stings prey using microscopic nematocysts.'),
    ('KANGAROO', 'Hopping Marsupial', 'Large Australian marsupial with powerful hind legs built for bounding hops.', 'Females carry developing joey offspring in an insulated abdominal pouch.'),
    ('KINGFISHER', 'Stream Diver', 'Brightly colored bird with a large dagger-shaped bill that dives for river fish.', "Its aerodynamic streamlined beak inspired the quiet nose shape of Japan's bullet trains."),
    ('KITTIWAKE', 'Cliff Gull', 'Small, gentle oceanic gull that nests exclusively on sheer vertical sea cliffs.', "Named for its loud, nasal 'kitti-waak' call echoing across breeding sea colonies."),
    ('KIWI', 'New Zealand Icon', 'Small flightless nocturnal bird with hair-like feathers and nostrils at bill tip.', 'The national emblem of New Zealand; lays an egg that is 20% of its body weight.'),
    ('KLIPSPRINGER', 'Rock Jumper', 'Small African antelope that stands on the tips of tiny cylindrical rubbery hooves.', 'Bounds effortlessly between isolated boulder pinnacles on rocky mountain slopes.'),
    ('KOALA', 'Eucalyptus Marsupial', 'Australian tree-dwelling marsupial with round ears and a large black nose.', 'Sleeps up to 20 hours a day because its diet of toxic eucalyptus leaves has low energy.'),
    ('KOI', 'Ornamental Carp', 'Colorful domesticated varieties of common carp kept in decorative garden ponds.', 'Prized in Japan as symbols of good fortune, perseverance, and long life.'),
    ('KOMODO', 'Giant Monitor Lizard', 'The largest living species of lizard, growing up to ten feet in length in Indonesia.', 'Hunts deer with powerful bites, serrated teeth, and anticoagulating toxic saliva.'),
    ('KOMODODRAGON', 'Monitor Lizard', 'The heaviest living lizard on Earth, growing over nine feet on Indonesian islands.', 'Hunts deer and water buffalo with serrated teeth and venomous anticoagulant bite.'),
    ('KRAIT', 'Venomous Elapid', 'Highly venomous nocturnal snake native to the Indian subcontinent and Southeast Asia.', 'Possesses potent neurotoxic venom, hiding beneath leaf litter and inside huts.'),
    ('KUDU', 'Spiral-Horned Antelope', 'African antelope species where males boast magnificent long corkscrew horns.', 'Possesses large sensitive ears and leaps over eight-foot fences with ease.'),
    ('LABRADOR', 'Water Retriever', 'Gentle, friendly water retriever dog breed with an otter-like swimming tail.', "Consistently ranked as the world's most popular family pet dog for decades."),
    ('LADYBUG', 'Spotted Beetle', 'Small round red or yellow beetle adorned with black spots that eats aphids.', "Gardener's ally; a single ladybug can devour thousands of destructive crop aphids."),
    ('LAMA', 'Woolly Camelid', 'Domesticated South American camelid valued as a reliable beast of burden.', 'Possesses a soft fleece coat and warns herds by sounding high-pitched alarms.'),
    ('LAPWING', 'Peewit Bird', "Crested wader with iridescent green plumage and a distinctive 'peewit' call.", 'Performs dramatic tumbling spring courtship aerobatics over agricultural fields.'),
    ('LARK', 'Singing Grassland Bird', 'Small terrestrial passerine bird celebrated for melodious singing in flight.', 'Skylarks sing complex, continuous warbling songs while hovering high in sky.'),
    ('LEATHERBACK', 'Giant Sea Turtle', 'The largest sea turtle in the world, lacking a bony shell and having leathery skin.', 'Dives over 4,000 feet deep into freezing ocean depths feeding strictly on jellyfish.'),
    ('LEMMING', 'Tundra Rodent', 'Small arctic rodent known for periodic population explosions on northern tundra.', 'Does not commit mass suicide; disperses in vast wandering numbers when food depletes.'),
    ('LEOPARD', 'Spotted Big Cat', 'Stealthy African and Asian feline celebrated for rosette spots and climbing agility.', 'Frequently drags heavy prey carcasses up into acacia trees to keep them from hyenas.'),
    ('LINNET', 'Finch', 'Small, slender finch where breeding males sport a crimson forehead and breast.', 'Feeds on seeds from dandelions and thistles, warbling melodious songs from hedges.'),
    ('LION', 'Apex Predator', "Majestic big cat known as the 'King of the Jungle' that lives in social prides.", 'Males possess a grand mane of fur; roars can be heard five miles away across savannas.'),
    ('LIZARD', 'Reptile', 'Widespread group of squamate reptiles with scaly skin, four legs, and movable eyelids.', 'Many species can detach their tail when grabbed by predators, later regrowing it.'),
    ('LLAMA', 'Andean Pack Animal', 'Domesticated South American camelid used as a pack animal in high Andes.', 'Social herd animal that communicates through humming and spits defensively.'),
    ('LOBSTER', 'Clawed Crustacean', 'Bottom-dwelling marine crustacean with large, muscular claws and hard exoskeleton.', 'Possesses a heavy crusher claw and a sharp cutter claw for eating mollusks.'),
    ('LOCUST', 'Swarming Grasshopper', 'Grasshopper species that enters a gregarious swarming phase in high populations.', 'Colossal swarms of billions can strip agricultural farmlands of crops in hours.'),
    ('LYNX', 'Northern Wild Cat', 'Medium-sized wild cat with triangular black ear tufts and snowshoe-like paws.', 'Specializes in hunting snowshoe hares across northern boreal forests in winter.'),
    ('MACAW', 'Vibrant Rainforest Bird', 'Large, long-tailed parrot native to Central and South America with brilliant plumage.', 'Possesses a powerful beak capable of cracking open rock-hard Brazil nuts.'),
    ('MACKEREL', 'Pelagic Swimmer', 'Streamlined, fast-swimming pelagic fish with iridescent green-blue barred backs.', 'Possesses a rich oily flesh, migrating in huge schools near the ocean surface.'),
    ('MALAMUTE', 'Arctic Sled Dog', 'Large, powerful arctic working dog breed bred to haul heavy freight sleds.', 'Possesses a dense double coat and immense endurance in sub-zero blizzards.'),
    ('MALLARD', 'Wild Duck', 'Common wild dabbling duck where males display glossy green heads and white collars.', 'The direct ancestor of almost all domesticated domestic duck breeds.'),
    ('MALTESE', 'Silky Toy Dog', 'Small toy dog breed covered in a long, flowing mantle of pure white silky hair.', 'Prized as a gentle lap companion since ancient Roman and Greek civilizations.'),
    ('MAMBA', 'Fast African Snake', 'Highly venomous, fast-moving African snake species renowned for potent neurotoxins.', 'The black mamba is named for the inky-black interior lining of its open mouth.'),
    ('MANATEE', 'Sea Cow', 'Gentle, slow-moving aquatic herbivore that grazes on underwater seagrass beds.', 'Can hold its breath underwater for up to 20 minutes while resting on river beds.'),
    ('MANDRILL', 'Colorful Baboon', 'The largest monkey in the world, with striking blue and red ridges on its face.', 'Dominant males sport vibrant blue and crimson facial markings and golden beards.'),
    ('MANTARAY', 'Gentle Giant Ray', 'Colossal filter-feeding ray with horn-like cephalic fins funneling plankton.', 'Can boast wingspans reaching 29 feet and frequently performs acrobatics above water.'),
    ('MANTIS', 'Praying Insect', 'Predatory insect with folded front raptorial legs held as if in prayer.', 'The only insect capable of turning its triangular head a full 180 degrees to track prey.'),
    ('MARE', 'Adult Female Horse', 'Mature female horse typically over four years of age.', 'Carries developing foals for an 11-month gestation period before giving birth.'),
    ('MARGAY', 'Arboreal Wildcat', 'Small spotted feline native to Central and South America with flexible ankles.', 'Can rotate its hind feet 180 degrees to run down tree trunks completely headfirst.'),
    ('MARMOT', 'Alpine Rodent', 'Large ground squirrel living in mountainous rocky terrain and high alpine meadows.', 'Whistles shrill alarm warnings to alert colony members of approaching golden eagles.'),
    ('MARSHTIT', 'Small Tit', 'Small woodland bird with a glossy black cap and tiny black bib under bill.', 'Caches thousands of seeds each autumn, remembering exact hiding spots months later.'),
    ('MARTEN', 'Arboreal Mustelid', 'Slender, agile mustelid adapted to living and hunting in coniferous tree canopies.', 'Leaps effortlessly between tree branches pursuing squirrels and nesting birds.'),
    ('MASTIFF', 'Gentle Giant Dog', 'Colossal, muscular working dog breed recognized for its massive head and jaw.', 'One of the heaviest dog breeds in the world, with adult males often exceeding 200 lbs.'),
    ('MEERKAT', 'Sentinel Forager', 'Small mongoose species living in underground burrows across the Kalahari Desert.', 'Takes turns standing upright on hind legs as sentinels watching skies for hawks.'),
    ('MEGAPODE', 'Mound Builder', 'Australian bird that incubates eggs in gigantic decomposing compost mounds.', 'Males use their bills as thermometers to test compost temperature, adding or removing leaf matter.'),
    ('MERLIN', 'Small Falcon', 'Small, fast falcon that hunts small songbirds through rapid, low-level flight.', "Historically known as the 'lady's hawk' in medieval falconry traditions."),
    ('MICE', 'Small Rodents', 'Small rodents with pointed snouts, round ears, and long scaly tails.', 'Prolific breeders that can produce dozens of offspring every single year.'),
    ('MILLIPEDE', 'Detritivore Arthropod', 'Slow-moving arthropod with two pairs of legs on most body segments, eating decaying leaves.', 'Curls into a tight defensive spiral and secretes foul-smelling fluids when disturbed.'),
    ('MINK', 'Semi-Aquatic Hunter', 'Sleek, dark-furred semi-aquatic carnivore valued for luxurious water-repellent fur.', 'Hunts fish, frogs, and waterfowl along riverbanks and lake shorelines.'),
    ('MINNOW', 'Small Fish', 'Small freshwater fish widely used as live bait by recreational anglers.', 'Forms dense coordinated schools in shallow streams to confuse aquatic predators.'),
    ('MOA', 'Extinct Giant', 'Extinct flightless bird of New Zealand that was hunted to extinction.', 'Some species grew over ten feet tall, grazing like woodland herbivores.'),
    ('MOLE', 'Subterranean Digger', 'Small subterranean mammal with paddle-like paws adapted for digging tunnels.', 'Nearly blind; locates earthworms using keen sensory snout whiskers.'),
    ('MONARCH', 'Flycatcher Bird', 'Tropical passerine bird characterized by agile aerial hawking and bold crests.', 'Inhabits forest canopies across Australasia, building tidy mossy cup nests.'),
    ('MONGOOSE', 'Snake Fighter', 'Quick, agile mammal renowned for its ability to fight and kill venomous cobras.', 'Possesses specialized acetylcholine receptor mutations granting partial venom immunity.'),
    ('MONKEY', 'Primate', 'Intelligent primate typically possessing a long tail and dexterous hands.', 'New World monkeys possess prehensile tails acting like a fifth grasping limb.'),
    ('MOORHEN', 'Water Hen', 'Black wetland bird with a distinctive bright red frontal shield above its beak.', 'Paddles across freshwater ponds, jerking its head rhythmically with each stroke.'),
    ('MOOSE', 'Largest Deer', 'The largest extant deer species, recognized by broad, palmate flat antlers.', 'Enjoys wading in marshy lakes to feed on nutrient-rich submerged aquatic weeds.'),
    ('MOSQUITO', 'Blood-Feeding Insect', 'Slender two-winged insect where females pierce skin to feed on blood proteins.', 'Vector for human diseases like malaria, yellow fever, and dengue virus.'),
    ('MOTH', 'Nocturnal Insect', 'Nocturnal winged insect covered in powdery scales with feathery antennae.', 'Navigates by the moon, causing it to spiral erratically around artificial lamps.'),
    ('MOUNTAINGOAT', 'Alpine Climber', 'Sure-footed white goat-antelope endemic to steep cliffs of western North America.', 'Scales near-vertical rock precipices using split hooves with rough traction pads.'),
    ('MUDPUPPY', 'Aquatic Salamander', 'Large fully aquatic salamander retaining bushy red external gills its entire life.', 'Inhabits murky rivers and lakes across eastern North America, active year-round.'),
    ('MULE', 'Equine Hybrid', 'Sturdy, sure-footed hybrid offspring of a male donkey and female horse.', 'Celebrated for endurance, calm temperament, and strength as a pack animal.'),
    ('MULLET', 'Jumping Fish', 'Coastal marine fish famous for leaping completely out of the water repeatedly.', 'Feeds on microscopic algae and detritus filtered from sandy bottom sediments.'),
    ('MUSKRAT', 'Aquatic Rodent', 'Medium-sized semi-aquatic rodent native to wetlands across North America.', 'Builds dome-shaped push-up houses from cattails, swimming with a flattened rudder tail.'),
    ('MYNA', 'Vocal Starling', 'Intelligent starling species native to Southern Asia renowned for vocal mimicry.', 'Hill mynas can mimic human speech with astonishing clarity and inflection.'),
    ('NARWHAL', 'Unicorn Whale', 'Arctic whale species where males possess a long, helical protruding tusk.', 'The tusk is actually a sensory canine tooth with millions of nerve endings.'),
    ('NAUTILUS', 'Chambered Cephalopod', 'Pelagic marine mollusk possessing a spiral partitioned shell and primitive pinhole eyes.', 'Adjusts buoyancy by regulating gas and liquid ratios inside shell chambers.'),
    ('NEWFOUNDLAND', 'Water Rescue Dog', 'Massive working dog breed with webbed feet and a water-resistant double coat.', 'Natural lifeguard dog renowned for instinctively rescuing drowning swimmers.'),
    ('NEWT', 'Semi-Aquatic Amphibian', 'Small, slender amphibian with a long tail that lives in ponds and woods.', 'Can regenerate fully functional limbs, eyes, and spinal cord tissue.'),
    ('NIGHTHERON', 'Nocturnal Fisher', 'Stocky, short-legged heron with red eyes and black crown that fishes at dusk.', "Stands motionless at water's edge waiting for fish and crabs to swim within reach."),
    ('NIGHTINGALE', 'Nocturnal Songster', 'Small plain brown songbird famous for its rich, melodious nocturnal singing.', 'Sings continuously through spring nights, celebrated in European poetry for centuries.'),
    ('NODDY', 'Tropical Tern', 'Tropical dark-plumaged tern that nests on oceanic coral atolls and sea cliffs.', 'Catches small fish driven to the ocean surface by hunting tuna schools.'),
    ('NUTCRACKER', 'Pine Seed Corvid', 'Spotted corvid specialized in harvesting and caching pine and hazel nuts.', 'Possesses a specialized sublingual pouch holding dozens of pine seeds at once.'),
    ('NUTHATCH', 'Tree Climber', 'Compact blue-grey woodland bird that can walk headfirst down tree trunks.', 'Wedges nuts into bark crevices before hacking them open with its sharp bill.'),
    ('NUTRIA', 'Coypu', 'Large semi-aquatic rodent native to South America with bright orange incisor teeth.', 'Inhabits freshwater marshes, digging burrows that can destabilize river levees.'),
    ('OCELOT', 'Small Spotted Cat', 'Medium-sized wild cat native to southwestern North America and South America.', 'Features patterned ring rosettes and large rounded ears with white spots.'),
    ('OCTOPUS', 'Eight-Armed Cephalopod', 'Soft-bodied, eight-armed cephalopod with remarkable camouflage capabilities.', 'Possesses three hearts, blue copper blood, and solves complex puzzles and mazes.'),
    ('OPOSSUM', 'American Marsupial', 'The only marsupial species native to North America north of the Rio Grande.', 'Feigns death by playing dead and releasing foul odors when cornered by predators.'),
    ('ORANGUTAN', 'Arboreal Great Ape', 'Red-haired great ape native to the rainforests of Borneo and Sumatra.', 'Spends nearly its entire life in trees, building a fresh sleeping nest each evening.'),
    ('ORCA', 'Killer Whale', 'Apex oceanic predator belonging to the dolphin family with black-and-white coloring.', 'Hunts in sophisticated family pods employing coordinated hunting tactics.'),
    ('ORIOLE', 'Songbird', 'Brilliantly colored songbird with bright yellow or orange and black plumage.', 'Constructs intricate woven hanging pouch nests suspended from slender tree branches.'),
    ('ORYX', 'Desert Antelope', 'Desert-dwelling antelope with long, straight spear-like horns and masked face.', 'Can endure intense heat by allowing its internal body temperature to rise safely.'),
    ('OSPREY', 'Fish Hawk', 'Fish-eating bird of prey featuring reversible outer toes and barbed foot pads.', 'Plunges feet-first into lakes and oceans to snatch slippery live fish.'),
    ('OSTRICH', 'Largest Living Bird', 'Colossal flightless African bird that can sprint at speeds up to 45 mph.', 'Lays the largest eggs of any living bird; possesses powerful defensive kicking legs.'),
    ('OTTER', 'Aquatic Mustelid', 'Playful semi-aquatic mammal with dense water-repellent fur and webbed feet.', 'Sea otters use smooth rocks as tools to crack open clams and sea urchins on bellies.'),
    ('OWL', 'Nocturnal Predator', 'Nocturnal bird of prey with forward-facing eyes, silent flight, and 270-degree neck turn.', 'Fringed wing feathers muffle the sound of air, enabling silent swoops on prey.'),
    ('OYSTERCATCHER', 'Chisel Wader', 'Stocky coastal wading bird with a bright orange-red chisel-like bill.', 'Uses its strong bill to pry open mussels, limpets, and oysters on rocky coasts.'),
    ('PALLASCAT', 'Steppe Cat', 'Small wild cat inhabiting Central Asian steppes with the densest fur of any cat.', 'Features low-set ears and flat pupils, stalking pikas across freezing rock screes.'),
    ('PANDA', 'Bamboo Bear', 'Iconic black-and-white bear native to mountain bamboo forests in central China.', 'Spends up to 14 hours every single day chewing through fibrous bamboo shoots.'),
    ('PANGOLIN', 'Scaly Insectivore', 'Solitary nocturnal mammal covered in large, overlapping keratin scales.', 'The only mammal with true scales; rolls into a tight ball when alarmed by predators.'),
    ('PANTHER', 'Melanistic Leopard', 'Melanistic color variant of leopards or jaguars with sleek black coats.', 'Possesses piercing yellow or green eyes and excels at nocturnal hunting.'),
    ('PAPILLON', 'Butterfly Spaniel', 'Toy spaniel named for its large, upright fringed ears resembling butterfly wings.', 'Remarkably agile and intelligent, frequently excelling in canine agility competitions.'),
    ('PARAKEET', 'Small Parrot', 'Small, slender parrot with a long, tapering tail and playful disposition.', 'Includes the Australian budgerigar, among the most popular pet birds worldwide.'),
    ('PARROT', 'Vocal Tropical Bird', 'Intelligent tropical bird with a curved beak, bright feathers, and zygodactyl feet.', 'Capable of mimicking human speech phrases and solving complex reasoning tests.'),
    ('PEACOCK', 'Iridescent Showman', 'Male peafowl celebrated for its extravagant, iridescent eye-spotted tail train.', 'Fans out its giant eye-spotted plumage train to attract female peahens in courtship.'),
    ('PECCARY', 'Javelina', 'Medium-sized pig-like mammal native to the Americas with sharp canine tusks.', 'Travels in tight social bands, foraging for prickly pear cacti in deserts.'),
    ('PEKINGESE', 'Lion Dog Breed', 'Ancient toy dog breed originating from imperial palaces in ancient China.', 'Bred to resemble Chinese guardian lions, pampered exclusively by Chinese emperors.'),
    ('PELICAN', 'Pouch Fisher', 'Large water bird with a long bill and an enormous throat pouch for scooping fish.', 'Dips its pouch into water to net schools of fish, draining gallons of water before swallowing.'),
    ('PENGUIN', 'Flightless Swimmer', 'Flightless aquatic bird wearing a black-and-white tuxedo coat native to Southern Hemisphere.', 'Flies underwater using powerful flipper wings, diving hundreds of feet deep for krill.'),
    ('PERSIAN', 'Long-Haired Cat', 'Ancient domestic cat breed characterized by a round flat face and long fluffy fur.', 'Quiet and gentle lap cat prized since Victorian times for luxurious grooming.'),
    ('PETREL', 'Tubenoser', 'Pelagic seabird that spends almost its entire lifespan wandering open oceans.', 'Features tubular nostrils on top of bill used to excrete excess ocean salt.'),
    ('PHALAROPE', 'Spinning Wader', 'Small shorebird that spins in tight circles on water to create feeding vortexes.', 'The spinning vortex pulls aquatic insect larvae up to the surface to be eaten.'),
    ('PHEASANT', 'Colorful Game Bird', 'Game bird native to Asia where males sport rich copper plumage and red eye patches.', 'Flushes into explosive vertical flight with loud wing clatter when surprised in brush.'),
    ('PIG', 'Domestic Ungulate', 'Highly intelligent omnivorous mammal with a flat cartilaginous snout.', 'Rolls in cool mud baths to regulate body temperature and deter bugs.'),
    ('PIGEON', 'Homing Bird', 'Stout-bodied bird with a small head renowned for extraordinary homing navigation.', 'Homing pigeons navigated carrying vital messages across battlefields in wartime.'),
    ('PIKE', 'Freshwater Hunter', 'Voracious predatory freshwater fish with needle-sharp teeth and duckbill snout.', 'Ambushes smaller fish and ducklings with explosive bursts of speed.'),
    ('PIPIT', 'Meadow Bird', 'Slender, streaked ground-dwelling bird that walks rather than hops across turf.', 'Meadow and tree pipits perform parachute singing display flights in spring.'),
    ('PIRANHA', 'Razor-Toothed Fish', 'South American freshwater fish famous for razor-sharp teeth and voracious schools.', 'Possesses extraordinarily strong jaws; feeds on fish, seeds, and fallen fruit.'),
    ('PLANTAIN', 'Banana Eater', 'Large African canopy bird with a stout bill belonging to the turaco family.', 'Leaps through fruit trees, feeding on wild figs, berries, and plantain fruits.'),
    ('PLATYPUS', 'Egg-Laying Mammal', 'Semi-aquatic monotreme possessing a duck-like bill, beaver tail, and webbed feet.', 'Males possess venomous ankle spurs; hunts aquatic larvae using electroreception.'),
    ('PLOVER', 'Shorebird', 'Compact shorebird with a short bill that runs in quick stops and starts on sand.', 'Lays cryptic speckled eggs directly in sandy scrapes, feigning broken wings if found.'),
    ('POCHARD', 'Diving Duck', 'Medium-sized diving duck with a rich chestnut-red head and silver-grey back.', 'Dives completely underwater to forage for submerged pondweeds and water insects.'),
    ('POLARBEAR', 'Arctic Apex Predator', 'The largest extant land carnivore, adapted for life on Arctic sea ice.', 'Possesses translucent hollow fur, black skin to absorb heat, and thick fat blubber.'),
    ('POMERANIAN', 'Fluffy Toy Dog', 'Tiny toy dog breed with an exuberant personality and thick puff-ball double coat.', 'Popularized by British royal figures including Queen Victoria in the 19th century.'),
    ('POODLE', 'Intelligent Water Dog', 'Highly intelligent dog breed with dense curly moisture-resistant coats.', 'Originally bred as duck-hunting water retrievers in Germany and France.'),
    ('PORCUPINE', 'Quilled Rodent', 'Rodent recognized by its protective coat of sharp, barbed defensive quills.', 'Cannot shoot its quills, but releases them easily upon contact with attacking predators.'),
    ('POSSUM', 'Australian Marsupial', 'Arboreal diprotodont marsupial with a prehensile tail and nocturnal habits.', 'Brush-tailed and ring-tailed species inhabit Australian suburban garden trees.'),
    ('PRAIRIEDOG', 'Colonial Rodent', "Burrowing ground squirrel that builds vast underground 'towns' across prairies.", 'Employs an extraordinarily complex vocal language with distinct calls for each predator.'),
    ('PRATINCOLE', 'Swallow Plover', 'Slender shorebird with long pointed wings that catches insects in flight like a swallow.', 'Hawks over marshlands at dusk, resting on flat dry mud during heat of day.'),
    ('PRAYINGMANTIS', 'Ambush Predator', 'Carnivorous insect holding spiked raptorial forelegs in a prayer-like posture.', 'Can swivel its triangular head 180 degrees, ambushing crickets and even hummingbirds.'),
    ('PROBOSCIS', 'Long-Nosed Monkey', 'Endangered monkey native to Borneo where males sport an enormous pendulous nose.', 'Excellent swimmer with partially webbed feet, crossing crocodile rivers in trees.'),
    ('PRONGHORN', 'Fastest North American Mammal', 'Antelope-like mammal capable of sustained running speeds reaching 55 mph.', 'The fastest land animal in the Western Hemisphere, outpacing all modern predators.'),
    ('PTARMIGAN', 'Snow Grouse', 'Arctic game bird whose feathered feet and plumage turn pure white in winter.', 'Burrows into soft snowdrifts to stay insulated from freezing howling blizzards.'),
    ('PUDU', 'Smallest Deer', 'The smallest deer species in the world, native to South American rainforests.', 'Stands only 14 inches tall, hiding from predators inside dense bamboo thickets.'),
    ('PUFFIN', 'Sea Parrot', 'Pelagic seabird featuring a large, brightly colored triangular beak in breeding season.', 'Flies underwater with flipper wings, carrying dozens of small fish lined up in its beak.'),
    ('PUG', 'Wrinkled Companion', 'Small dog breed characterized by wrinkled faces, short snouts, and curled tails.', 'Bred as pampered lapdogs for ancient Chinese emperors and European royalty.'),
    ('PUMA', 'American Big Cat', 'Solitary wild cat native to the Americas, also known as mountain lion.', 'Leaps up to 40 feet horizontally when ambushing deer in rocky canyons.'),
    ('PYTHON', 'Constrictor Snake', 'Non-venomous constrictor snake that wraps coils around prey to restrict blood flow.', 'Can unhinge flexible jaw ligaments to swallow prey larger than its own head whole.'),
    ('QUOKKA', 'Smiling Marsupial', 'Small round-eared marsupial native to Rottnest Island near Western Australia.', "Dubbed the 'happiest animal in the world' due to its friendly expression in selfies."),
    ('RACCOON', 'Masked Forager', 'Medium-sized mammal native to North America with a black eye mask and ringed tail.', 'Features dexterous front paws allowing it to pry open trash cans and unlatch doors.'),
    ('RACER', 'Swift Snake', 'Fast, slender non-venomous colubrid snake widespread across North America.', 'Relies on speed and keen eyesight to flee predators or pursue frogs and mice.'),
    ('RAM', 'Male Sheep', 'Adult male sheep armed with large spiral curling defensive horns.', 'Charges competing rival males at 20 mph during autumn breeding ruts.'),
    ('RATTLESNAKE', 'Viper with Rattle', 'Pit viper possessing a tail rattle made of interlocking keratin segments.', 'Vibrates its tail rattle up to 50 times per second to warn intruders before striking.'),
    ('RAY', 'Flat Fish', 'Cartilaginous fish with broad pectoral fins that ripple like underwater wings.', 'Closely related to sharks; glides gracefully over sandy shallow seabeds.'),
    ('RAZORBILL', 'Black-and-White Auk', 'Deep-diving seabird with a thick, blunt black bill marked by vertical white lines.', 'Swims underwater with powerful wing beats, diving hundreds of feet for sandeels.'),
    ('REDPANDA', 'Tree Forager', 'Small arboreal mammal with reddish-brown fur, a ringed tail, and white markings.', 'Native to the eastern Himalayas; uses its bushy tail to wrap itself for warmth.'),
    ('REDPOLL', 'Arctic Finch', 'Small brownish-grey finch displaying a bright red cap patch on its forehead.', 'Survives bitter sub-zero arctic winters by caching birch seeds inside throat pouches.'),
    ('REDSHANK', 'Marsh Sentinel', 'Wading bird with bright orange-red legs whose alarm calls alert entire marshes.', "Known as the 'warden of the marshes' because it shrieks alarm at any intruder."),
    ('REDSTART', 'Chat Bird', 'Slender insectivorous bird with a constantly quivering bright orange-red tail.', 'Catches flying insects on the wing, bobbing its vibrant tail upon landing.'),
    ('REDWING', 'Winter Thrush', 'Small migratory thrush recognized by a rusty-red patch under each wing.', "Migrates at night; its thin 'seep' flight calls can be heard in autumn night skies."),
    ('REINDEER', 'Arctic Deer', 'Arctic and subarctic deer species where both males and females grow antlers.', 'Also known as caribou; features specialized hooves adapted for walking on snow.'),
    ('RETRIEVER', 'Water Fetch Dog', 'Hunting dog breed bred to retrieve game birds safely without tooth marks.', 'Includes Golden and Labrador Retrievers, among the most popular family pets globally.'),
    ('RHINO', 'Horned Giant', 'Massive horned herbivore with thick protective dermal armor skin folds.', 'Horns are made of keratin—the same protein found in human hair and fingernails.'),
    ('RHINOCEROS', 'Armored Giant', 'Massive horned ungulate with thick armor-like skin folds and poor eyesight.', 'Horns are made of compressed keratin fibers, the same protein as human nails.'),
    ('ROADRUNNER', 'Chaparral Bird', 'Fast-running ground cuckoo native to southwestern deserts of North America.', 'Can sprint at 20 mph, hunting venomous rattlesnakes, scorpions, and tarantulas.'),
    ('ROBIN', 'Red-Breasted Songbird', 'Beloved garden bird with a bright orange-red breast and inquisitive nature.', 'Follows gardeners turning over soil to snatch freshly unearthed earthworms.'),
    ('RODENT', 'Gnawing Mammal', 'Mammal characterized by a single pair of continuously growing incisors in jaws.', 'Accounts for roughly 40% of all mammal species found across the globe.'),
    ('ROLLER', 'Colorful Bird', 'Old World bird named for aerial acrobatics and rolling dives performed in flight.', 'Possesses brilliant turquoise and blue plumage, catching large insects on the wing.'),
    ('ROOK', 'Colonial Corvid', 'Black corvid bird nesting in noisy treetop colonies known as rookeries.', 'Distinguished from crows by the bare grey skin around the base of its bill.'),
    ('ROOKERY', 'Bird Colony', 'Dense communal breeding colony of rooks, penguins, or marine seals.', 'Provides safety in numbers against ground predators during egg incubation.'),
    ('ROTTWEILER', 'Drover Mastiff', 'Robust, powerful working dog breed historically used to herd cattle.', 'Known for its loyalty, strength, and black coat with rich tan markings.'),
    ('SAINTBERNARD', 'Alpine Rescue Dog', 'Colossal Swiss working dog breed historically bred for mountain rescue at hospice.', 'Rescued lost, freezing travelers trapped in deep snowdrifts in the Great St Bernard Pass.'),
    ('SALAMANDER', 'Tailed Amphibian', 'Lizard-like amphibian with moist skin, a long tail, and four equal-length legs.', 'Inhabits damp rotting forest logs, breathing through skin or feathery gills.'),
    ('SAMOYED', 'Smiling White Dog', 'Fluffy white arctic herding dog breed bred by Siberian nomadic tribes.', "Features an upturned 'Samoyed smile' that prevents icicles forming on lips."),
    ('SANDCAT', 'Desert Feline', 'Small wild cat living in arid deserts with fur-covered paws that insulate from hot sand.', 'Can survive without drinking water, obtaining all required hydration from prey.'),
    ('SANDGROUSE', 'Desert Water Carrier', 'Arid-zone bird whose breast feathers can soak up water like a sponge.', 'Flies 50 miles to water holes, soaking breast feathers to fly water back to chicks.'),
    ('SANDPIPER', 'Shore Runner', 'Small wading bird that probes sandy ocean shores for crustaceans between waves.', 'Sprints rapidly back and forth following the ebb and flow of breaking ocean surf.'),
    ('SARDINE', 'Small Oily Fish', 'Small, silvery epipelagic fish belonging to the herring family.', 'Packed into dense bait balls in the annual South African sardine run.'),
    ('SCORPION', 'Stinging Arachnid', 'Predatory arachnid featuring grasping pincers and a curved tail with a venomous stinger.', 'Fluoresces brilliant glowing neon blue-green under ultraviolet black light.'),
    ('SEAANEMONE', 'Flower Invertebrate', 'Sedentary marine predatory polyp with stinging tentacles resembling a garden flower.', 'Provides a stinging protective home for immune clownfish in coral reef communities.'),
    ('SEACUCUMBER', 'Benthic Invertebrate', 'Leathery marine invertebrate that scavenges organic debris from ocean floors.', 'Can expel its internal organs defensively through self-evisceration when attacked.'),
    ('SEAGULL', 'Coastal Scavenger', 'Common coastal seabird recognized by grey-and-white plumage and loud squawking.', 'Opportunistic forager that catches fish and boldly scavenges picnic scraps.'),
    ('SEAHORSE', 'Equine Fish', 'Small marine fish with a horse-like head, prehensile tail, and armor plates.', 'Males possess a specialized brood pouch where they fertilize and carry developing eggs.'),
    ('SEAL', 'Pinniped Swimmer', 'Semi-aquatic marine mammal with sleek flippers adapted for agile swimming.', 'Hauls out onto rocky shores and arctic ice floes to bask and rear pups.'),
    ('SEALION', 'Eared Pinniped', 'Marine pinniped with visible external ear flaps and rotating hind flippers for walking.', 'Highly agile on land; barks loudly while hauling out in noisy coastal colonies.'),
    ('SEAOTTER', 'Tool-Using Mustelid', 'Marine mammal with dense water-repellent fur that floats on its back in kelp beds.', 'Wraps itself in giant kelp fronds while sleeping so it does not drift away into currents.'),
    ('SEASNAKE', 'Pelagic Reptile', 'Venomous marine snake with a paddle-shaped tail and flattened body for swimming.', 'Possesses highly potent neurotoxic venom, absorbing oxygen through its skin underwater.'),
    ('SEAURCHIN', 'Spiny Marine Ball', 'Globular spiny echinoderm that grazes on marine kelp forests on rocky seabeds.', "Moves slowly using hundreds of tiny tube feet and five-toothed Aristotle's lanterns."),
    ('SERVAL', 'Long-Legged Cat', 'Slender African wild cat with exceptionally long legs and oversized radar ears.', 'Uses acute hearing to detect rodents burrowing underground before leaping 9 feet high.'),
    ('SETTER', 'Bird Hunting Dog', "Type of gundog bred to locate game birds by crouching or 'setting' on scent.", 'Includes Irish, English, and Gordon Setters with silky feathered coats.'),
    ('SHARK', 'Cartilaginous Fish', 'Ancient apex marine predator possessing a skeleton made of flexible cartilage.', 'Equipped with multiple rows of replaceable teeth and ampullae electroreceptors.'),
    ('SHEARWATER', 'Pelagic Glider', 'Medium-sized petrel that shears across wave crests with stiff wings.', 'Nests in burrows on offshore islands, flying thousands of miles on foraging trips.'),
    ('SHEPHERD', 'Pastoral Dog', 'Working dog breed developed specifically to guard and drive flocks of sheep.', 'German Shepherds excel in police work, search-and-rescue, and military roles.'),
    ('SHIBA', 'Japanese Brushwood Dog', 'Spirited, fox-like Japanese hunting dog breed with a curled tail and prick ears.', "Famous for its independent personality, cleanliness, and iconic 'Shiba scream'."),
    ('SHIHTZU', 'Chrysanthemum Dog', 'Compact companion dog breed with a short muzzle and luxurious floor-length coat.', 'Bred in Tibetan monasteries and gifted to Chinese royalty as royal lap warmers.'),
    ('SHOEBILL', 'Whale-Headed Stork', 'Colossal prehistoric-looking African marsh bird with a massive shoe-shaped bill.', 'Stands motionless for hours before lunging forward to clamp down on lungfish.'),
    ('SHREW', 'Tiny Insectivore', 'Tiny, mouse-like mammal with a pointed snout, small eyes, and frantic metabolism.', 'Must consume up to its entire body weight in insects every 24 hours to stay alive.'),
    ('SHRIKE', 'Butcherbird', 'Predatory songbird with a hooked raptor-like bill that impales prey on thorns.', 'Stores insects, lizards, and mice on barbed wire fences to eat later in larder caches.'),
    ('SHRIMP', 'Small Crustacean', 'Small decapod crustacean swimming backwards using tail flicks across oceans.', 'Crucial food source for larger fish, whales, seabirds, and human cuisine.'),
    ('SIAMESE', 'Pointed Cat Breed', 'Distinctive Asian cat breed with slender bodies, striking blue eyes, and color points.', 'Known for highly vocal, conversational meows and affectionate loyalty.'),
    ('SISKIN', 'Yellow Finch', 'Small, agile finch with yellow-green plumage and a deeply notched tail.', 'Hangs upside down from spruce and alder cones to extract tiny tree seeds with bill.'),
    ('SKINK', 'Smooth Lizard', 'Lizard characterized by smooth, glossy scales and short, reduced limbs.', 'Blue-tongued skinks puff up and flash an azure tongue to frighten off predators.'),
    ('SKUA', 'Fierce Seabird', 'Powerful, aggressive seabird that preys upon penguin eggs and chicks.', 'Attacks human researchers who venture too close to its tundra ground nesting sites.'),
    ('SKUNK', 'Defensive Mammal', 'Black-and-white patterned mammal capable of spraying noxious defensive liquids.', 'Ejects foul-smelling sulfurous secretions up to ten feet from anal scent glands.'),
    ('SLOTH', 'Slow Canopy Dweller', 'Tree-dwelling tropical mammal famous for slow movements and upside-down hanging.', 'Features algae-tinted green fur providing camouflage high in rainforest trees.'),
    ('SLUG', 'Shell-Less Mollusk', 'Gastropod mollusk lacking an external protective shell, moving on slime.', 'Secretes hygroscopic mucus that protects its moist body from drying out.'),
    ('SNAPPER', 'Reef Fish', 'Marine ray-finned fish known for large canine teeth and bright red coloration.', 'Red snappers are prized commercial catches inhabiting rocky reefs in the Gulf of Mexico.'),
    ('SNAPPINGTURTLE', 'Freshwater Turtle', 'Freshwater turtle with powerful hooked jaws and a saw-toothed tail.', 'Alligator snappers possess a pink, worm-like tongue lure to attract curious fish.'),
    ('SNIPE', 'Camouflaged Wader', 'Secretive marshland wader with cryptic brown plumage and a very long bill.', "Makes an eerie 'drumming' or 'bleating' sound using vibrating outer tail feathers in dive."),
    ('SNOWLEOPARD', 'Ghost of the Mountains', 'Solitary big cat native to rugged mountain ranges of Central Asia.', 'Possesses a long, thick furry tail used for balance and wrapped around the face for warmth.'),
    ('SOLE', 'Flat Bottom Fish', 'Flatfish living on sandy sea bottoms with both eyes on its right side.', 'Blends seamlessly into ocean sediments using active chromatophore camouflage.'),
    ('SPANIEL', 'Gun Dog', 'Type of gun dog bred to flush game birds out from dense brush and wetlands.', 'Encompasses Cocker, Springer, and Cavalier King Charles Spaniel varieties.'),
    ('SPARROW', 'City Bird', 'Small, adaptable brown songbird common in urban cities and farmlands worldwide.', 'Thrives alongside human settlements, foraging for breadcrumbs and weed seeds.'),
    ('SPHYNX', 'Hairless Cat Breed', 'Cat breed known for its lack of fur, large ears, and wrinkled skin.', 'Warm to the touch; requires periodic sponge baths to absorb natural skin oils.'),
    ('SPIDER', 'Eight-Legged Weaver', 'Eight-legged predatory arachnid that spins intricate silk webs to snare flying insects.', 'Silk proteins are pound-for-pound stronger than steel and exceptionally elastic.'),
    ('SPIDERMONKEY', 'Prehensile Primate', 'Primate with long spindly limbs and an agile prehensile tail with a tactile pad.', 'Swings through South American rainforest canopies like a gymnast using its tail.'),
    ('SQUID', 'Ten-Limbed Cephalopod', 'Fast-swimming cephalopod with eight arms, two tentacles, and bilateral fins.', 'Giant squid possess the largest eyes in the animal kingdom, measuring a foot wide.'),
    ('SQUIRREL', 'Bushy-Tailed Rodent', 'Agile bushy-tailed tree rodent famous for caching acorns for winter survival.', 'Features sharp curved claws allowing it to run down tree trunks completely headfirst.'),
    ('SQUIRRELMONKEY', 'Canopy Primate', 'Small, agile New World monkey living in massive social canopy troops.', 'Features high brain-to-body mass ratio and communicates via bird-like chirps.'),
    ('STAG', 'Adult Male Deer', 'Mature adult male deer bearing an impressive set of branching bony antlers.', 'Bellows loudly to challenge rival bucks during autumn breeding seasons.'),
    ('STARFISH', 'Sea Star', 'Marine invertebrate with radiating arms, tube feet, and central digestive disk.', 'Can regenerate lost arms; pries open clams before pushing its stomach outward.'),
    ('STARLING', 'Murmuration Bird', 'Iridescent speckled bird celebrated for massive swirling aerial flock dances.', 'Thousands of starlings execute fluid, synchronized murmuration patterns at dusk.'),
    ('STILT', 'Extremely Long Legs', 'Wading bird with black-and-white plumage and impossibly long pink legs.', 'Has the longest legs relative to body size of any bird other than flamingos.'),
    ('STINGRAY', 'Flat Cartilaginous Fish', 'Flattened cartilaginous fish with broad pectoral fins that undulate like wings.', 'Possesses a venomous barbed spine on its tail used strictly in self-defense.'),
    ('STOAT', 'Short-Tailed Weasel', 'Small mustelid whose brown summer coat turns completely snowy white in winter.', 'Known as ermine when in pure white winter pelage with a black-tipped tail.'),
    ('STONECHAT', 'Heathland Bird', 'Small chat whose sharp call sounds like two pebbles being knocked together.', 'Pairs stay together year-round on coastal heaths and moorlands.'),
    ('STORK', 'Migratory Wader', 'Large, long-legged wader famous in folklore for delivering newborn babies to doorsteps.', 'Nests atop chimney stacks and telephone poles in European villages.'),
    ('STURGEON', 'Ancient Armored Fish', 'Ancient cartilaginous bony fish covered in five rows of bony scutes.', 'Females take decades to mature; prized for harvesting black culinary caviar.'),
    ('SUGARGLIDER', 'Gliding Marsupial', 'Small nocturnal gliding possum with a gliding membrane extending from wrists to ankles.', 'Glides up to 150 feet between forest trees to feed on sweet acacia gum and nectar.'),
    ('SUNBIRD', 'Old World Nectar Bird', 'Small, brilliantly iridescent tropical bird that feeds on floral nectar.', 'The Old World ecological counterpart to the hummingbirds of the Americas.'),
    ('SWALLOW', 'Aerial Feeder', 'Small bird with streamlined wings and a deeply forked tail catching bugs in flight.', 'Builds mud cup nests beneath the eaves of barns and cliff overhangs.'),
    ('SWALLOWTAIL', 'Fork-Tailed Butterfly', 'Large, colorful butterfly featuring distinct tail extensions on its hindwings.', 'Caterpillars possess an orange forked scent gland called an osmeterium for defense.'),
    ('SWAN', 'Graceful Waterfowl', 'Large, elegant waterfowl with long curved necks and pristine white or black plumage.', 'Pairs mate for life and engage in synchronized courtship dance routines on lakes.'),
    ('SWORDFISH', 'Billfish', 'Predatory billfish featuring a long, flat bill resembling a broadsword.', 'Slashes at schools of squid and mackerel with its bill to stun them before eating.'),
    ('TAIPAN', 'Deadly Snake', 'Large, fast-moving and highly venomous elapid snake native to Australia.', 'The inland taipan possesses the most toxic venom of any reptile on planet Earth.'),
    ('TAPIR', 'Forest Herbivore', 'Large herbivorous mammal with a short, prehensile snout living in tropical forests.', 'Excellent swimmer that retreats into deep river water when pursued by big cats.'),
    ('TARANTULA', 'Hairy Spider', 'Large, hairy arachnid that hunts at night without spinning aerial capture webs.', 'Kicks irritating urticating hairs from its abdomen to deter approaching predators.'),
    ('TARPON', 'Silver King', 'Large, silvery game fish capable of breathing air using a modified swim bladder.', 'Revered by sports anglers for ferocious fighting leaps when hooked on fly rods.'),
    ('TASMANIAN', 'Carnivorous Marsupial', 'Stocky carnivorous marsupial with black fur and an ear-splitting screech.', 'Possesses one of the strongest bite forces relative to body size of any mammal on Earth.'),
    ('TENREC', 'Madagascar Wonder', 'Diverse family of small mammals native to Madagascar resembling hedgehogs and shrews.', 'The streaked tenrec rubs specialized quills together to produce sound via stridulation.'),
    ('TERMITE', 'Wood-Eating Insect', 'Social insect that feeds on cellulose and builds massive desert mounds.', 'Harbors symbiotic gut protozoa capable of digesting tough dead wood fibers.'),
    ('TERN', 'Graceful Seabird', 'Slender seabird with long pointed wings and a deeply forked tail.', 'The Arctic tern flies from the Arctic to Antarctic and back annually.'),
    ('TERRAPIN', 'Brackish Turtle', 'Small turtle living in fresh or brackish water with diamond-patterned shell plates.', 'Diamondback terrapins inhabit coastal tidal salt marshes along Atlantic coasts.'),
    ('TERRIER', 'Feisty Hunter', 'Type of dog breed originally bred to hunt vermin, rats, and burrowing pests.', 'Known for tenacious courage, wiry coats, and energetic personalities.'),
    ('THRUSH', 'Vocal Songbird', 'Songbird with a spotted breast celebrated for rich, flute-like melodic songs.', 'Smashes hard snail shells against favorite garden rocks called anvils to eat meat.'),
    ('TICK', 'Blood Parasite', 'Eight-legged arachnid parasite that latches onto hosts to feed on blood.', 'Can transmit bacterial pathogens such as Lyme disease through its saliva.'),
    ('TIGER', 'Striped Big Cat', 'The largest extant cat species, instantly recognizable by dark vertical stripes.', 'Excellent swimmers who often bathe in rivers and lakes to cool down in tropical heat.'),
    ('TIGERSHARK', 'Striped Predator', 'Large apex shark recognized by dark vertical stripes on young and voracious appetite.', "Known as the 'wastebasket of the sea', swallowing fish, turtles, and even license plates."),
    ('TILAPIA', 'Cichlid Fish', 'Freshwater cichlid fish native to Africa and widely cultivated in aquaculture.', 'Hardy and fast-growing; feeds on algae and plant matter in warm farm ponds.'),
    ('TINAMOU', 'Ancient Ground Bird', 'Ancient ground bird related to ostriches that lays glossy porcelain-colored eggs.', 'Eggs look like polished ceramic jewels in shades of turquoise, purple, and green.'),
    ('TIT', 'Small Songbird', 'Small, active woodland songbird that flits between tree branches for seeds.', 'Includes chickadees, blue tits, and great tits frequenting garden bird feeders.'),
    ('TOAD', 'Dry-Skinned Amphibian', 'Terrestrial amphibian characterized by dry, warty skin and short hopping legs.', 'Possesses parotoid glands behind the eyes that secrete bitter defensive toxins.'),
    ('TORTOISE', 'Terrestrial Shelled Reptile', 'Land-dwelling reptile with elephantine feet and a high, domed protective shell.', 'Galapagos tortoises can live well over 150 years on sparse volcanic islands.'),
    ('TOUCAN', 'Giant-Billed Bird', 'Neotropical bird famous for its massive, brightly colored, lightweight bill.', 'Uses its huge bill to reach distant fruit on branches and regulate body temperature.'),
    ('TREECREEPER', 'Bark Forager', 'Small brown mottled woodland bird that spirals up tree trunks searching for bark bugs.', 'Uses its stiff woodpecker-like tail feathers as a prop while climbing.'),
